{"name":"Frugal","hex":"#a5d7b2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"frugal","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":[": Careful or wise in expenditure; avoiding waste.",": Obtained by or characterized by frugality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frugal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Frugality","blocks":[{"text":"Frugality is the quality of being frugal, sparing, thrifty, prudent, or economical in the consumption of resources, whether they be food, time, or money. It involves the avoidance of waste, extravagance, and lavishness."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Temperance_Enjoying_a_Frugal_Meal_MET_DP818490.jpg/330px-Temperance_Enjoying_a_Frugal_Meal_MET_DP818490.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frugality","wikidata":"Q1858477"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/280-broadway.jpg/500px-280-broadway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/280-broadway.jpg/500px-280-broadway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"280 Broadway, the first department store in the United States","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A280-broadway.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/PuritanGallery.jpg/330px-PuritanGallery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/PuritanGallery.jpg/330px-PuritanGallery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gallery of famous 17th-century Puritan theologians: Thomas Gouge, William Bridge, Thomas Manton, John Flavel, Richard Sibbes, Stephen Charnock, William Bates, John Owen, John Howe and Richard Baxter","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org